</Section>

<Section id="printinganArrayList">

## 4. Printing an ArrayList

We can print the ArrayList directly, whereas, for Arrays, we need to convert it into a `String` to print.

#### Code

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;

class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ArrayList<String> players = new ArrayList<>();

        players.add(0, "Bryant");
        players.add("Wade");

        System.out.println(players); // Printing the ArrayList.
    }
}
```

