## Introduction

In the previous units, we learned HashSets and performed some basic operations like adding elements, removing elements, etc.

In this unit, we will learn some special operations on HashSets like union, intersection, etc.

## 1. Union

The `addAll()` method can be used to perform the union of two sets.

#### Syntax

```java
hset1.addAll(hset2);
```

Here, the `addAll()` method mutates `hset1` and adds all the unique elements from the `hset2` to the `hset1`

#### Code

```java
import java.util.HashSet;

class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        HashSet<Integer> hset1 = new HashSet<>();
        HashSet<Integer> hset2 = new HashSet<>();
        hset1.add(3);
        hset1.add(32);
        hset1.add(8);
        hset2.add(8);
        hset2.add(32);
        hset2.add(30);

        System.out.println("hset1: " + hset1);
        System.out.println("hset2: " + hset2);

        hset1.addAll(hset2); // union of hset1 and hset2

        System.out.println("\nhset1 after Union:  " + hset1);
    }
}
```

#### Output

```
hset1: [32, 3, 8]
hset2: [8, 32, 30]

hset1 after Union:  [32, 3, 8, 30]
```

