## 2. Intersection

The `retainAll()` method can be used to perform the intersection of two sets.

#### Syntax

```java
hset1.retainAll(hset2);
```

Here, the `retainAll()` method retains all the elements that are common in `hset1` and `hset2` and removes all the other elements from the `hset1`.

#### Code

```java
import java.util.HashSet;

class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        HashSet<Integer> hset1 = new HashSet<>();
        HashSet<Integer> hset2 = new HashSet<>();
        hset1.add(3);
        hset1.add(32);
        hset1.add(8);
        hset2.add(8);
        hset2.add(32);
        hset2.add(30);

        System.out.println("hset1: " + hset1);
        System.out.println("hset2: " + hset2);

        hset1.retainAll(hset2); // intersection of hset1 and hset2

        System.out.println("\nhset1 after Intersection:  " + hset1);
    }
}
```

#### Output

```
hset1: [32, 3, 8]
hset2: [8, 32, 30]

hset1 after Intersection:  [32, 8]
```

