## 3. Difference

The `removeAll()` method can be used to find the difference between two sets.

#### Syntax

```java
hset1.removeAll(hset2);
```

Here, the `removeAll()` method removes all the elements that are common in `hset1` and `hset2` and retains all the other elements in `hset1`.

#### Code

```java
import java.util.*;

class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        HashSet<Integer> hset1 = new HashSet<>();
        HashSet<Integer> hset2 = new HashSet<>();

        hset1.add(3);
        hset1.add(32);
        hset1.add(8);

        hset2.add(8);
        hset2.add(24);
        hset2.add(30);

        System.out.println("hset1: " + hset1);
        System.out.println("hset2: " + hset2);

        hset1.removeAll(hset2); // difference of hset1 and hset2

        System.out.println("\nhset1 after Difference:  " + hset1);
    }
}
```

#### Output

```
hset1: [32, 3, 8]
hset2: [8, 24, 30]

hset1 after Difference:  [32, 3]
```

