>     flat_discount = 0
>     min_bill = 100
>
>     @classmethod
>     def update_flat_discount(cls, new_flat_discount):
>         cls.flat_discount = new_flat_discount
> ```
>
> </details>

The `main()` method should be always defined with `public` and `static` keywords in order to be accessible for the Java Virtual Machine (JVM) to call the `main()` method.

<MultiLineNote>

JVM acts as a run-time engine to run Java applications. In Java code, it is the JVM that actually calls the `main()` method

</MultiLineNote>

### 2.1 Accessing Class Methods

The class methods can also be accessed using the dot (`.`) notation. We can access the class methods directly using the class name. There is no need to create instances to access the class attributes.

The objects of the class and instance methods can also access the class methods.

