## Introduction

In the previous unit, we learned the concepts like inheritance and composition in Java.

In this unit, we'll learn the method overriding, different types of inheritance, and more about `super` keyword, etc.

## 1. Method Overriding

Similar to Python, we can override methods in Java. Method overriding allows a subclass to provide a specific implementation of a method that its superclass already provides.

When a method in a subclass has the same name, parameters, and return type as a method in its superclass, then the subclass's method is said to override the superclass's method.

#### Code

```java
class Animal {
    void eat() {
        System.out.println("Animal is eating");
    }
}

class Horse extends Animal {
    void eat() {  // overrides the eat() method of Animal class
        System.out.println("Horse is eating");
    }
}

class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
