<br/>

When a method is overridden,

- calling that method using the parent object (superclass object) invokes the method in the parent class.
- calling that method using the child object (subclass object) invokes the method in the child class.

#### Code

```java
class Animal {
    void eat() {
        System.out.println("Animal is eating");
    }
}

class Horse extends Animal {
