The `final` keyword can be used for methods also. A method declared with `final` is called a final method.

The purpose of creating the final methods is to restrict the unwanted and improper use of method definition while overriding the method.

The final methods cannot be overridden.

#### Syntax

```java
final returnType methodName() {
    // body of the method
}
```

